      "vendoredSha256": "4171b03bbe3280ffa990db17e8c5433bbc7c5a685dd9e90580789b5ec773e5ec",
      "delta": "Inject caller-owned line-process spawn; pass explicit env unchanged; preserve server ids and support replies; default/per-request timeouts; bounded held and pending state with fatal overflow; release timers on settlement, failed write, exit and kill. S2b: settlement consumer errors reject already-dequeued waiters; no uncaught timer failure. Re-vendor: omit upstream home queue and executable diagnostics; preserve direct injected ownership and bounded exitError; retain handled spawned promise. Native replies await acknowledged stdin writes under bounded ownership. 0.33.1 re-vendor: MCP credential redaction of error and exit text through the caller-owned exitError. 0.37.0 re-vendor: killTree is not passed, because the caller-owned spawn owns tree termination; an exit or kill settles pending requests as exited (budget overflow stays error) and the owned transport reports the exit after stdout closes, so pending entries are not kept for late replies; error replies carry the redacted native error. 0.44.0 re-vendor: keep the explicit string env without the upstream sessionEnvironment merge; omit upstream resources, because the injected LineProcess has no resources reader. 0.54.3 re-vendor: take the upstream Pending method, the undefined-waiter guard and the nativeErrorCause error cause (method and redacted native error); the BYOK transport seams stay."
    },
