      "vendoredSha256": "57cbdc48ad3aaa12577e686d02a873f25f93958c3acbdc959e805c18511d1a0e",
      "delta": "Pass configurable control deadline (default 30000ms) and record typed RPC timeouts as rejected responses. Use an equivalent deferred Promise compatible with the SDK ES2022 lib. S2b: replace the redundant deferred response waiter with synchronous response capture to avoid hanging on required-consumer/budget failure. 0.37.0 re-vendor: keep the synchronous capture with the upstream fallback takeover, exited outcome and late-reply frame; a failed takeover record rejects the control and never escapes the fallback timer. 0.54.3 re-vendor: take the upstream SessionNotFoundError for a thread/resume that codex answers -32600 \"no rollout found for thread id\", the resumeId parameter and the direct native cause; the timeout and synchronous response capture stay."
    },
    {
      "path": "runtimes/codex/session.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/runtimes/codex/session.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "bf4002166b8fb92d791bd175494ae98a1947ee763244f64cf3538b17e2b29659",
      "vendoredSha256": "2834122ede1e8b5405521b9f2ae8b55c6ba9bfee83616e2a3b2cc276b54c2326",
      "delta": "BYOK S2a: injected spawn and explicit filtered env; caller-selected sandbox (danger-full-access default, inherit passes no override); raw AdapterSession without sealSession/input-images; native-first frame capture with visible fold failure/kill; bounded server request decline/reject using 0.159.2 response schemas; ES2022 deferred Promise. S2b: explicit body.origin=byok-native; inject required consumer/budget before registration. Re-vendor: remove capabilities.steer; refine optional generic steer to a required Codex method; no withdraw or derived deliver. Native interactions: explicit on-request policy with readback, opt-in caller-owned request lifecycle, one-shot typed replies and local cancellation records; no fallback allow or persistence. Native replies await acknowledged stdin writes under bounded ownership. 0.33.1 re-vendor: build the open request before the owned spawn and pass its redactor to the client. 0.37.0 re-vendor: take the upstream abort fallback; its kill and the server-request deadline timer never throw out of the timer. 0.44.0 re-vendor: take the upstream input-delivery fold, steer acceptance record and MCP tool denials; options.env stays a complete string environment, so no value is a null removal; steer keeps caller-owned image admission; omit upstream resources. 0.54.3 re-vendor: build sessionCredentialRedactor once per open in place of upstream withSessionCredentials/sealSession; redact retained records through the kernel hook, errors thrown from the open path and from prompt, steer, queue, abort and dispose; pass options.resume to openThread; derive graph nodes from record envelopes and carry kernel.link events on the derived frame, with no kernel.node."
    },
